    [1;31mBACKPORT[m: sched/core: Fix reset-on-fork from RT with uclamp
    
    uclamp_fork() resets the uclamp values to their default when the
    reset-on-fork flag is set. It also checks whether the task has a RT
    policy, and sets its uclamp.min to 1024 accordingly. However, during
    reset-on-fork, the task's policy is lowered to SCHED_NORMAL right after,
    hence leading to an erroneous uclamp.min setting for the new task if it
    was forked from RT.
    
    Fix this by removing the unnecessary check on rt_task() in
    uclamp_fork() as this doesn't make sense if the reset-on-fork flag is
    set.
    
    [ qperret: [1;31mBACKPORT[m because of a conflict with the Android-specific
      SUGOV_RT_MAX_FREQ sched_feat, which is equally unnecessary in this
      path ]
    
